{
    "$schema": "Declares which files to bundle into the editor toolchain for WASM compilation.",
    "engine": {
        "root_files": ["CMakeLists.txt"],
        "directories": [
            "cmake",
            "tools",
            "src/esengine"
        ]
    },
    "third_party": {
        "root_files": ["CMakeLists.txt"],
        "full": [
            "stb",
            "nlohmann",
            "cute_tiled",
            "yoga"
        ],
        "partial": {
            "glm": ["glm"],
            "spine-runtimes-2.1": ["spine-c/src", "spine-c/include"],
            "spine-runtimes-3.8": ["spine-c/spine-c/src", "spine-c/spine-c/include"],
            "spine-runtimes-4.1": ["spine-c/spine-c/src", "spine-c/spine-c/include"],
            "spine-runtimes-4.2": [
                "spine-cpp/spine-cpp/src", "spine-cpp/spine-cpp/include",
                "spine-c/spine-c/src", "spine-c/spine-c/include"
            ],
            "spine-runtimes-4.3": ["spine-cpp/src", "spine-cpp/include"]
        }
    },
    "native": {
        "$comment": [
            "The two projects the native host links that are too large to vendor. PINNED, not",
            "tracked: `--depth 1` of a moving branch makes a runtime template unreproducible, and",
            "webgpu.h is a moving target. Not submodules either — Dawn fetches its own dependencies",
            "with a script rather than submodules, so tracking it that way saves nobody the fetch",
            "while putting a multi-GB clone in front of everyone who only builds for the web.",
            "`node build-tools/cli.js native --fetch-deps` checks both out at these commits."
        ],
        "dawn": {
            "repo": "https://dawn.googlesource.com/dawn",
            "commit": "296a00d20c4324d0a0363096ab23da4bf4f26d35"
        },
        "quickjs": {
            "repo": "https://github.com/quickjs-ng/quickjs",
            "commit": "3d3cf3d86b66551403745a5b06acbed2b0f31dfd"
        },
        "sdl": {
            "$comment": [
                "The desktop window, event loop, gamepads and IME (release-3.4.14). Desktop only:",
                "iOS and Android already have an OS event loop the host drives, and adding a second",
                "one there would be a rewrite of two working platforms to no end.",
                "Pinned to the tag's COMMIT, like the other two — a tag is a moving ref, and a",
                "runtime template other people install has to rebuild to the same bytes."
            ],
            "repo": "https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL",
            "commit": "147a8ee32dbf9ac02f3794964490687b6bbda1bc"
        }
    },
    "cmake": {
        "version": "3.31.7",
        "platforms": {
            "darwin": {
                "filename": "cmake-${version}-macos-universal.tar.gz",
                "strip_prefix": "cmake-${version}-macos-universal/CMake.app/Contents"
            },
            "win32": {
                "filename": "cmake-${version}-windows-x86_64.zip",
                "strip_prefix": "cmake-${version}-windows-x86_64"
            },
            "linux-x64": {
                "filename": "cmake-${version}-linux-x86_64.tar.gz",
                "strip_prefix": "cmake-${version}-linux-x86_64"
            },
            "linux-arm64": {
                "filename": "cmake-${version}-linux-aarch64.tar.gz",
                "strip_prefix": "cmake-${version}-linux-aarch64"
            }
        }
    }
}
